# #1099 prototype: the same steps against a WPF TextBox body and a hosted RichEdit body.
# The prototype opens with the message body focused.
w 4
# Give NVDA a focus change in this window before the test (a relaunch can leave it on the old one).
q +{TAB}
w 2
q {TAB}
w 3

# 1. Typed-word echo (#300, #906): each word as Space ends it, and the last as Enter ends it.
t one two three
w 3
e one
e two
k {ENTER}
w 3
e three

# The rest of the text, typed without logging.
Q Alpha line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Beta line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Gamma
q {ENTER}
Q A much longer line of text here
q {ENTER}
Q Short
q {ENTER}
Q End
w 3

# 2. Down from the top: each line once, blank lines as blank (#891).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
e This line has a bold word
k {DOWN}
w 3
e one two three
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Beta
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Gamma
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Gamma

# 3. From the end of a long line, Down onto a shorter one: that line alone.
k {DOWN}
w 3
e A much longer line of text here
k {END}
w 2
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Short
e! End

# 4. Ctrl+Down / Ctrl+Up by paragraph (#1077).
k ^{HOME}
w 3
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e one two three
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Gamma
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e blank
k ^{DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
e! Gamma
k ^{UP}
w 3
e blank
k ^{UP}
w 3
e Alpha line
e! Beta

# 5. Focus between the To box and the body.
k +{TAB}
w 3
e To
k {TAB}
w 3
e Message body
